  "readme": "# Original failed episode-10 short-voice run and bounded source-connection audit\n\nThe original saved episode-10 scene10450058 route5→6→7 run (session62388) exited1 and remains failed. There is no terminal acceptance. The player progressed normally and the retained original channel emitted one play/playing/ended, with source Opus bytes matching the published asset. These are limited mechanical facts, independently reviewed; they do not replace the original failed outcome or accept source timing, gain, listening, acting or the whole episode.\n\nTwo helper errors were recorded: expected production URL construction retained local port5198, and HTTP304 Not Modified was marked as a redirect. The included two-source fixes received independent static review only. They were not executed by this publication and are not a complete new executable kit. Original helper sources, raw failure/traces, full prepared programme, historical inventory, and root/independent closure evidence are retained losslessly. The historic all-inputs-exact statement applies to its026a run, before later native voice/character publications. No private process-inventory listings are copied.\n\nThe Opus check reproduces quantitative correspondence to the original WAV/source. A one-sample difference at48kHz remains recorded without an invented explanation. This numerical result is not listening or complete speech acceptance.\n\nThe chapter1 audit covers31 sections/routes excluding the first three:119 explicit source/target scene pairs have existing effective directory edges. It found no directly installable missing connection. The119 pairs and120 positive-target FINISH objects match the earlier sealed catalogue; unknown choices, missing scripts and target-free endings stay explicit. This is a data/source audit, with no new DOM/SVG visibility or continuous-route claim.\n\nThis commit adds only this audit directory. Production native scripts, review rows, assets, source code and deployment are unchanged. Every payload has original/stored byte counts and SHA256; gzip members are lossless representations. Original exit1 and all limitations remain authoritative.\n\nThe first unpublished archive failed git diff --check because original Firefox/FFmpeg log bytes contain whitespace. That failure and the complete first archive are preserved locally; this version stores those logs losslessly as gzip, without normalizing evidence.\n"
